course: dictionary
lesson: 12034
title: Putting events in order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Chronological means arranged in the order in which things happened, from the earliest to the latest. The word comes from the Greek word for time, so it is all about when things happen.
explain: «First we ate breakfast, then we brushed our teeth, and finally we left for school.» These events are in chronological order, because each one happens after the one before it. Time words like first, then and finally help you see the order.
explain: Historians put events on a timeline in chronological order. Writers do the same when they tell what happened on a trip or write about a famous person's life.
explain: Think about your own day. If you told the story of it in chronological order, a listener could follow it easily. If the events were jumbled, the story would be hard to follow.
fact: Chronological means arranged in the order in which things happened, from earliest to latest.
fact: «Chronological order» means putting events, dates or steps in time order.
fact: «In reverse chronological order» means starting with the latest event and going back to the earliest.
fact: A timeline is a line that shows events in chronological order.
fact: Time words such as «first», «next», «then» and «finally» help show chronological order in a story.
exercise: «First she planted the seed, then she watered it, and finally the flower grew.» Is this in chronological order? | Only if it is written as a poem | *Yes, each step happens after the one before | No, there are no time words at all | No, the flower grew first
exercise: Put these in chronological order: wake up, eat breakfast, go to bed. Which happens first? | Eat breakfast | They all happen at the same time | Go to bed | *Wake up
exercise: Which word means arranged in the order things happened? | Numerical | Alphabetical | Hilarious | *Chronological
test: «The rocket launched, then it reached space, and later it landed safely.» Which word shows the order of these events? | Launched | *Then | Rocket | Safely
test: Which list is in chronological order for a birthday party? | Cut the cake, sing happy birthday, arrive at the party | Cut the cake, arrive at the party, sing happy birthday | Sing happy birthday, arrive at the party, cut the cake | *Arrive at the party, sing happy birthday, cut the cake
exam: Which phrase means events in time order, starting with the latest and going back to the earliest? | Chronological order | Random order | Alphabetical order | *Reverse chronological order
